															<img width="2560" height="1707" src="https://schweidandsons.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/schweid-and-sons-cuts-of-beef-blog-featured-image-scaled.jpg" class="bg wp-post-image" alt="" decoding="async" fetchpriority="high" srcset="https://schweidandsons.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/schweid-and-sons-cuts-of-beef-blog-featured-image-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://schweidandsons.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/schweid-and-sons-cuts-of-beef-blog-featured-image-300x200.jpg 300w, https://schweidandsons.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/schweid-and-sons-cuts-of-beef-blog-featured-image-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://schweidandsons.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/schweid-and-sons-cuts-of-beef-blog-featured-image-768x512.jpg 768w, https://schweidandsons.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/schweid-and-sons-cuts-of-beef-blog-featured-image-150x100.jpg 150w, https://schweidandsons.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/schweid-and-sons-cuts-of-beef-blog-featured-image-600x400.jpg 600w, https://schweidandsons.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/schweid-and-sons-cuts-of-beef-blog-featured-image-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://schweidandsons.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/schweid-and-sons-cuts-of-beef-blog-featured-image-2048x1365.jpg 2048w, https://schweidandsons.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/schweid-and-sons-cuts-of-beef-blog-featured-image-640x427.jpg 640w, https://schweidandsons.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/schweid-and-sons-cuts-of-beef-blog-featured-image-400x267.jpg 400w" sizes="(max-width: 2560px) 100vw, 2560px" />														<div class="title-wrap">
								<h1 class="title">Best Cuts of Beef for Burgers: Expert Guide to Juicy, Flavorful Patties</h1>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- Blog Content -->
		<article class="blk_row theme_light" aria-label="Blog content">
			<div class="blk_col_wrap">
				<div class="blk_container type-grid">
					<div class="col-24">
						<div class="mdl_wysiwyg_a">
							<div class="content">
								<p>When it comes to crafting the perfect Burger, the meat blend matters just as much as the seasoning or the sear. At Schweid &amp; Sons, we believe in starting with high-quality, whole muscle cuts—not leftover trim—to deliver a consistently delicious Burger every time. But <strong>different cuts of meat</strong> act differently—some contribute bold flavor, while others lend juiciness or structure.</p>
<p>Let’s discuss the <strong>best cuts of meat for Burgers</strong>, why specific cuts are chosen, and how different combinations can impact the final result.</p>
<h2>Fat vs. Function: The Best Beef For Burgers</h2>
<p>Cows, like people, use different muscles in different ways. Overworked muscles—like those from the shoulder (chuck) or hindquarter (round)—are naturally tougher due to their dense muscle fibers. They often have a bolder flavor but need to be balanced with more tender, fatty cuts to keep the Burger juicy and palatable.</p>
<p>On the other hand, underused muscles—like those near the ribs or belly—are typically more tender and carry more intramuscular fat (marbling). These are ideal for grinding because they create a Burger that&#8217;s both flavorful and juicy.</p>
<p>This is where the art of blending comes into play. By combining different cuts of beef—i.e. lean, flavorful cuts with fattier, tender ones—you get a balanced Burger that’s juicy, meaty, and satisfying. So remember: choosing the best meat for Burgers isn&#8217;t just about fat percentage—it’s about <em>where</em> that fat comes from and how it works with the lean.</p>
<h2>Common Cuts Used in Burger Blends</h2>
<p>Let’s dive into the best meat for grinding Burgers that’ll wow your guests:</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://schweidandsons.com/blog/highlight-the-cut-chuck/"><strong>Chuck</strong></a> is the backbone of many Burger blends. When ground, the cut works well alone, or can be elevated when blended with another cut of beef. It&#8217;s high marbling gives the Burger a rich and buttery beef flavor.</li>
</ul>
<p><img decoding="async" class="alignnone wp-image-35810 size-medium" src="https://schweidandsons.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Steer-Chuck-300x200.jpg" alt="chuck beef location on steer" width="300" height="200"></p>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://schweidandsons.com/blog/the-art-of-the-burger-blend-brisket-cut/"><strong>Brisket</strong></a> is a hardworking muscle from the lower chest. Brisket has two main muscles, the flat and the point. The flat is relatively lean, but it has a strong beefy flavor and a coarse grind texture that adds a hearty bite. The point muscle has more marbling, leading to a rich flavor in your Burger. When balanced with other cuts, brisket becomes a powerful backbone in a blend.</li>
</ul>
<p><img decoding="async" class="alignnone wp-image-35815 size-medium" src="https://schweidandsons.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Steer-Brisket-300x200.jpg" alt="cut of brisket beef location on a steer" width="300" height="200"></p>
<ul>
<li>Cut from the chuck and rib section, <a href="https://schweidandsons.com/blog/the-art-of-the-burger-blend-short-rib/"><strong>short rib</strong></a> offers rich marbling and intense flavor. It’s prized for its buttery texture and ability to create a luscious, juicy Burger. Because of its fat content, it helps balance leaner cuts beautifully. Just don’t overdo it—too much fat can result in a greasy Burger.</li>
</ul>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="alignnone wp-image-35816 size-medium" src="https://schweidandsons.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Steer-Short-Rib-300x200.jpg" alt="cut of sirloin beef location on the steer" width="300" height="200"></p>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://schweidandsons.com/blog/the-art-of-the-burger-blend-grass-fed-standard/"><strong>Sirloin</strong></a> comes from the hip and is moderately tender with a clean, beefy flavor. It’s not as fatty as rib or brisket, but it adds structure and depth to any blend. It’s often used to add volume without overpowering the other cuts.</li>
</ul>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="alignnone wp-image-35817 size-medium" src="https://schweidandsons.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Steer-Sirloin-300x200.jpg" alt="cut of sirloin beef location on a steer" width="300" height="200"></p>
<ul>
<li>The <a href="https://schweidandsons.com/blog/the-art-of-the-burger-blend-round-beef/"><strong>round</strong></a> is a lean cut from the rear leg that is high in protein but low in fat. On its own, it can be dry—but it brings firmness and bite to a blend. When paired with rich cuts like short rib or chuck, it offers a great textural contrast.</li>
<li><a href="https://schweidandsons.com/blog/the-art-of-the-burger-blend-hanger/"><strong>Hanger steak</strong></a> is a lesser-known cut from the plate (near the diaphragm), and it’s considered a “butcher’s cut” because of its flavor. It has a bold, slightly gamey taste that can add a certain <em>je ne sais quois</em> to your blend. However, it must be used carefully, as its grain and chewiness can dominate if overused.</li>
<li><strong><a href="https://schweidandsons.com/blog/new-product-announcement-the-ribeye-blend/">Ribeye</a> </strong>is a premium cut from the rib primal, known for its rich marbling and tender texture. It brings a luxurious, steakhouse-style flavor to any Burger blend. Thanks to its high fat content, ribeye adds incredible juiciness and depth—but like short rib, it should be balanced with leaner cuts to avoid an overly fatty patty.</li>
</ul>
<h2>What Happens When You Change the Percentages?</h2>
<p>Adjusting the ratios of each cut can dramatically change the eating experience of a Burger. For example:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>More brisket</strong> = if using the lean portion, it leads to a denser, beefier Burger with a slightly coarse bite.</li>
<li><strong>More short rib or ribeye</strong> = a juicier, more indulgent Burger with rich, beefy flavor.</li>
<li><strong>More round or sirloin</strong> = a firmer texture and leaner taste.</li>
<li><strong>Touch of hanger</strong> = a savory, umami-rich background note.</li>
</ul>
<p>At Schweid &amp; Sons, our blending process is based on experience, experimentation, and a commitment to consistency—because one extra percent of fat or lean can mean the difference between a dry patty and one that melts in your mouth.</p>
<h2>Explore Our Burger Blends</h2>
<p>Whether you’re grilling for a crowd or savoring a solo stack, we’ve got the perfect Burgers for your plate:</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://schweidandsons.com/product/the-all-american/"><strong>The All American Blend</strong></a><strong> – Chuck (75/25).</strong> Classic, juicy, and well-balanced. This all-Chuck blend is what most people picture when they think of the perfect backyard Burger—rich in flavor, tender, and reliably delicious. Also available in <a href="https://schweidandsons.com/product/c-a-b-all-american/">100% Certified Angus Beef®</a>.</li>
</ul>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="alignnone wp-image-36643 size-large" src="https://schweidandsons.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/02/Schweid-Sons-the-all-american-1024x683.png" alt="schweid and sons the all american made from premium cuts of 100% angus chuck beef" width="1024" height="683" srcset="https://schweidandsons.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/02/Schweid-Sons-the-all-american-1024x683.png 1024w, https://schweidandsons.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/02/Schweid-Sons-the-all-american-300x200.png 300w, https://schweidandsons.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/02/Schweid-Sons-the-all-american-768x512.png 768w, https://schweidandsons.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/02/Schweid-Sons-the-all-american-150x100.png 150w, https://schweidandsons.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/02/Schweid-Sons-the-all-american-600x400.png 600w, https://schweidandsons.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/02/Schweid-Sons-the-all-american-1536x1024.png 1536w, https://schweidandsons.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/02/Schweid-Sons-the-all-american-2048x1365.png 2048w, https://schweidandsons.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/02/Schweid-Sons-the-all-american-640x427.png 640w, https://schweidandsons.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/02/Schweid-Sons-the-all-american-400x267.png 400w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></p>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://schweidandsons.com/product/the-one-percenter/"><strong>The One Percenter</strong></a><strong> – Chuck (75/25).</strong> A luxurious take on the classic Chuck Burger, made exclusively with Certified Angus Beef® Brand Prime Chuck—something only 3% of US cattle can aspire to. Tender and juicy with exceptional mouthfeel, this blend offers rich, crowd-pleasing flavor.</li>
</ul>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="alignnone wp-image-36655 size-large" src="https://schweidandsons.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/02/schweid-and-sons-the-one-percenter-1024x640.png" alt="schweid and sons certified angus beef the one percenter made from premium cuts of prime chuck" width="1024" height="640" srcset="https://schweidandsons.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/02/schweid-and-sons-the-one-percenter-1024x640.png 1024w, https://schweidandsons.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/02/schweid-and-sons-the-one-percenter-300x188.png 300w, https://schweidandsons.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/02/schweid-and-sons-the-one-percenter-768x480.png 768w, https://schweidandsons.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/02/schweid-and-sons-the-one-percenter-150x94.png 150w, https://schweidandsons.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/02/schweid-and-sons-the-one-percenter-600x375.png 600w, https://schweidandsons.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/02/schweid-and-sons-the-one-percenter-1536x960.png 1536w, https://schweidandsons.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/02/schweid-and-sons-the-one-percenter-2048x1280.png 2048w, https://schweidandsons.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/02/schweid-and-sons-the-one-percenter-640x400.png 640w, https://schweidandsons.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/02/schweid-and-sons-the-one-percenter-87x55.png 87w, https://schweidandsons.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/02/schweid-and-sons-the-one-percenter-400x250.png 400w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></p>
<ul>
